  "full_text": "For a hill men would kill why they do not know. Stiffened wounds test their pride. Men of five still alive through the raging glow. Gone insane from the pain that they surely know. Take a look to the sky just before you die. It's the last time you will. Blackened roar, stiffened roar fills the endless cry. Fills the soul with the ruthless crack of dawn. Empty roar with a ruthless cry. Here's the silence so loud. Nothing more except the will to be what will be. Blinded eyes do see. And on through the ecstasy. Here's the silence so loud. Crack of dawn through the agony. What will be, what will be, what will be, what will be.",
